Name: IndicXlit
Short Name: indicxlit
URL: https://github.com/AI4Bharat/IndicXlit
Version: e7049fe725b11c0a187d42edeb2f56aa1ffee5fd
Date: 2022-07-03
License: MIT
License File: LICENSE
Security Critical: no
Shipped: yes

Description:
AI4Bharat's IndicXlit, a 6+6 layer fairseq transformer (11.5M parameters) that
transliterates Latin text into 21 Indian scripts. Tark runs it on the device
to type Indian-language words in the address bar. Only the model weights and
the vocabulary are used; the word-frequency dictionaries AI4Bharat publishes
are not shipped. The weights are MIT licensed (README, paper and Hugging Face
card). Version is the commit of huggingface.co/ai4bharat/IndicXlit,
indicxlit-en-indic-v1.0/transformer/indicxlit.pt, sha256
2f03fe0dfb2edc40f3c11f9293c4feda4fa8ed5366fec2981391606f224a09f7. The
vocabulary comes from corpus-bin/dict.en.txt and dict.hi.txt of the same
commit.

Local Modifications:
Converted to Tark's TXLM v1 fp16 blob (xlit-model.bin) by utils/xlit_convert.py:
weights stored as fp16, optimiser state and position buffers dropped, the
vocabulary written into the blob header. No change to the model's behaviour
beyond fp16 rounding.
